qe:
Find out the output of the following code:
void main()
{ int num1=10, num2=20, num3;
  num3 = num1 > 2 + num2 != 3;
  printf("%d", num3); }

expe:
✔ In SQL SELECT * FROM table_name; returns all columns; * means 'all columns'.
📌 For chosen columns write SELECT name, age FROM student;
✖ SELECT ALL concerns duplicate rows, not all columns; SELECT FROM without columns is an error.

exp:
✔ SELECT DISTINCT परिणाम से डुप्लिकेट पंक्तियाँ हटाकर केवल अद्वितीय पंक्तियाँ दिखाता है, जैसे SELECT DISTINCT city FROM student;
📌 डिफॉल्ट SELECT (ALL) डुप्लिकेट सहित सभी पंक्तियाँ देता है।
✖ NODUPLICATE और ELIMINATE SQL कीवर्ड नहीं हैं।

expe:
✔ SELECT DISTINCT removes duplicate rows and shows only unique rows, e.g. SELECT DISTINCT city FROM student;
📌 The default SELECT (ALL) returns all rows including duplicates.
✖ NODUPLICATE and ELIMINATE are not SQL keywords.
